## Versioning and releases

`pyproject.toml` is the source of truth for the extension version. Update it with
`uv version` and create a matching `vX.Y.Z` tag to release.

CI overwrites `[extension].version` in `src/{{ identifier }}/manifest.toml` before
testing and publishing. The committed manifest version is an initial value; it
does not need to be updated manually. Run `python scripts/sync_version.py` before
local testing or loading the extension into CFMS.

`python scripts/build_extension.py` also synchronizes the manifest before creating
`dist/{{ identifier }}-<version>.zip` and its SHA-256 checksum. The release workflow
checks the tag, project version, manifest, archive, and checksum before publishing.
